{"page":776,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.05257,"w":0.42424,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"762 Chapter 13: Vector-Valued Functions and Motion in Space"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.09343,"w":0.58893,"h":0.02816,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"where g is the acceleration due to gravity. We find r as a function of t by solving the fol- lowing initial value problem."},{"x":0.39448,"y":0.13087,"w":0.19884,"h":0.02141,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Differential equation: d2r"},{"x":0.57305,"y":0.13881,"w":0.06956,"h":0.02235,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dt2 = -gj"},{"x":0.39449,"y":0.16808,"w":0.29447,"h":0.02153,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"Initial conditions: r = r0 and dr"},{"x":0.67489,"y":0.17462,"w":0.16029,"h":0.02074,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"dt = v0 when t = 0"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.20599,"w":0.16825,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The first integration gives"},{"x":0.55621,"y":0.23714,"w":0.01543,"h":0.0128,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dr"},{"x":0.55757,"y":0.24368,"w":0.12188,"h":0.02074,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dt = -(gt)j + v0."},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.27505,"w":0.17403,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"A second integration gives"},{"x":0.53567,"y":0.30639,"w":0.05319,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"r = - 1"},{"x":0.58068,"y":0.312,"w":0.11924,"h":0.02142,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"2gt2j + v0t + r0."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.34409,"w":0.44774,"h":0.01433,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Substituting the values of v0 and r0 from Equations (3) and (4) gives"},{"x":0.46154,"y":0.37545,"w":0.0532,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"r = - 1"},{"x":0.50656,"y":0.38106,"w":0.27004,"h":0.02142,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"2gt2j + (y0 cos a)ti + (y0 sin a)tj + 0. (++++++)++++++*"},{"x":0.6612,"y":0.40676,"w":0.01761,"h":0.01433,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"v0t"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.4298,"w":0.17027,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Collecting terms, we have"},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.48834,"w":0.23009,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Ideal Projectile Motion Equation"},{"x":0.47659,"y":0.51501,"w":0.23976,"h":0.02579,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"r = (y0 cos a)ti + a(y0 sin a)t - 1"},{"x":0.70817,"y":0.51501,"w":0.17381,"h":0.03044,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"2gt2bj. (5)"},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.58962,"w":0.59302,"h":0.04417,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Equation (5) is the vector equation of the path for ideal projectile motion. The angle a is the projectile’s launch angle (firing angle, angle of elevation), and y0, as we said before, is the projectile’s initial speed. The components of r give the parametric equations"},{"x":0.44593,"y":0.64466,"w":0.31909,"h":0.02238,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"x = (y0 cos a)t and y = (y0 sin a)t - 1"},{"x":0.75683,"y":0.65027,"w":0.15542,"h":0.02142,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"2gt2, (6)"},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.6817,"w":0.55161,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"where x is the distance downrange and y is the height of the projectile at time t Ú 0."},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.71905,"w":0.59297,"h":0.02984,"fs":0.01407,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 4 A projectile is fired from the origin over horizontal ground at an initial speed of 500 m>sec and a launch angle of 60°. Where will the projectile be 10 sec later?"},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.7621,"w":0.59297,"h":0.02899,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Solution We use Equation (5) with y0 = 500, a = 60°, g = 9.8, and t = 10 to find the projectile’s components 10 sec after firing."},{"x":0.40267,"y":0.80239,"w":0.23976,"h":0.02579,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"r = (y0 cos a)ti + a(y0 sin a)t - 1"},{"x":0.63425,"y":0.80239,"w":0.0451,"h":0.03044,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"2gt2bj"},{"x":0.41739,"y":0.84204,"w":0.07116,"h":0.02323,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"= (500)a1"},{"x":0.48037,"y":0.84204,"w":0.32204,"h":0.03044,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"2b(10)i + a(500)a 23 2 b10 - a1 2b(9.8)(100)bj"},{"x":0.41739,"y":0.88121,"w":0.12058,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"≈2500i + 3840j"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.90747,"w":0.58893,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Ten seconds after firing, the projectile is about 3840 m above ground and 2500 m down- range from the origin."}]}